After last week's update that brought a slew of major changes, we're rolling out a small batch of patches, smoothing out a few UI issues and introducing a handful of fixes. 

UI: 
Train list station filter contains player's color marker for multiplayer sessions;

James Hall's portrait is now shown properly in Chapter five;

Oil power plant earnings effect is now shown properly when upgrading;

Fixes:
Trains now pass crossroads properly;

Restarting of a mission in a campaign now keeps skill points;

Bank and Power plants earnings count properly in multiplayer sessions;

Oil well capacity fixed in certain missions;

Gameplay:
Oil Power Plant and Coal Power Plant buildings added to the game; 

Produced electricity can now be sold to citizens or used in production; 

Chemical Factory now consumes electricity to produce fertilizers and chemicals; 

Chemicals are now required to produce Dynamite in an Explosives Plant; 

Dynamite can be used to restore exhausted mines; 

Clay pits have unlimited deposits but require electricity for deeper extraction; 

Oil wells are now unlimited, but deeper pumping increases upkeep; 

Competitive Mode is now available for generated multiplayer maps; 

Added resource capacity scenario options for multiplayer maps; 


Balancing:
City Hall's internal consumption rate has been reduced; 

Contracts for produced commodities will now appear later; 

Banks provide services to a limited number of citizens on a monthly basis; 


UI:
Full/empty notifications can be managed per warehouse; 

Alt+Click on commodities now sets the correct number of carriages in the route planner; 

Added a "Delete All Old Save Files" button; 

Fixed 'researched' symbol for Geology map cells; 

While a train is selected, clicking on a city or a commodity on the map will always add it to the train's route. 


Fixes: 
Trains now move against road direction if the path was set before the semaphore switched; 

Bridge pillars no longer disappear on long bridge; 

Bridge and tunnels were not built properly in some cases; 

Players can not launch auctions before building an office; 

Localization improvements.


Please note that, due to the significant changes made in this update, we've run into another (this time, smaller) issue when it comes to your save files. While post-mission save files will be still be compatible, those made during a mission will not. Just like last time, you'll still be able to access the previous version through a separate branch, to tie up any loose deals.

Balancing:
Cities will now buy local commodities with less intensity to prevent early depletion;

Office staff will now have positive and negative skills more often;
Fixes:
Video card driver updates now work properly;

Misleading "failed" text for objective will not appear now;

Some geology staff skills not show proper effects values;

Farm building cannot be constructed in Chapter 5;

Sausage Factory building cannot be constructed in Chapter 5;

Cotton fields now consume fertilizers;

Achievements will now be issued according to completed chapter;

Depleted cross marker now has a proper material;

Railroad construction particle effects optimized;

Localization improvements.

We’re thrilled to share the another update for the game! This time, we’re introducing user-generated scenarios!

Gameplay

 Added map generator options for Single player and Multi player;
 Added special beginning options to generated scenarios;
 Added City Hall local consumption behavior;
 An ending save file will be created after each chapter is completed in the campaign;
Balancing

 Grain and Cotton added to Geology resources and now can be discovered;
 Wood logging added to city lobbying in non-campaign scenarios;
 Consolidation locomotive rebalanced;
 Mastodon locomotive rebalanced;
 Warehouses of one player can now be used by other players in a multiplayer cooperative mode;
 Lobbyist level requirements for 'This or That' lobbying have been changed;
UI

 Notifications added to a Top panel when a research/lobbying/geology is completed;
 A Multiplayer saved session is now loaded from a main Load Game dialog;
 Cargo list scroll has been added to a Train panel;
 Auction panel improvements in a multiplayer versus mode;
 Discovered resources via geology are now visible to all players;
 Custom save, Autosave and Quick save naming refactored;
 Other UI improvements;
Fixes

 A special case when save file stuck loading at 72%;
 Objectives deadline is now synced properly in a multiplayer session;
 Building transaction fly-ups are now visible on a client;
 Locomotive broken on the way state is now synced properly in a multiplayer session;
 Locomotive animation was not working  properly in some cases;

 Localization improvements.

Hey everyone, 

As the Early Access phase of Railroad Corporation 2 is slowly chugging along, we’ll be steadily updating you about patches in these short blogs and on our Steam Discussions thread. 

We’re thrilled to let you know that today, we’re bringing you some key fixes and improvements, directly addressing some of the areas you’ve highlighted since launch. Thanks to your detailed feedback, we’ve focused on resolving a few pesky issues, and making sure everything runs smoother for everyone. 

Here’s a full breakdown of our most recent patch notes:


Fixed an error that could cause a save files stopped loading at 72%;
Fixed an error caused wide screen resolution options missing in settings;
Fixed an error that did not allow create a trading rules in buildings created as a result of a geology discovery;
Fixed an error that caused a city population reset at a certain conditions;
Localization improvements.


This is just the beginning of our post-launch journey together, and we’re committed to keeping the momentum going. So please keep sharing your insights as we continue to make Railroad Corporation 2 the best experience it can be!

